   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6r0u",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "I'll be the committed and effective advocate this electorate deserves. Mt Albert should be an affordable place to live. Local voters have strongly supported the Greens with their party vote in recent elections, knowing that we have the solutions needed to tackle big issues like the cost of living and climate change. This year, it's a four-way race, and you can vote for the candidate that best represents you."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6r2p",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I'll bring my experience as an effective advocate and legislator to serve the electorate and ensure no one is left behind. In my second term I have successfully supported locals with a range of issues, reunited migrant families, championed a bill to stop supermarkets from charging excessive prices, and held the Government to account over wrongful welfare cuts predominantly affecting sick, injured and disabled people. I'll be an accessible and committed MP for Mt Albert."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6r4k",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Reduce the price of essentials; food, power, housing, so that we can all live affordable lives."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6r6f",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Create flood resilient, well-planned neighbourhoods where families have access to nature."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6r8a",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Support our local economy by reducing taxes for 96% of New Zealanders and taxing the super rich."
     }
    ],
