   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6qbx",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "As a Mt Albert local for 40 years, I understand the needs of our people. To deliver better infrastructure, more community spaces, and solutions for high energy, transport and food prices, Mt Albert needs a local champion. I'm in politics for a fairer New Zealand: 25 years in employment law left me frustrated with changing the law one case at a time. So far in Parliament, I've introduced legislation to improve workers' and renters' rights."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6qds",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "As an employment lawyer, I spent my career listening to people's stories, understanding their concerns and standing up for their rights. As MP for Mt Albert, my role is to be a strong voice for our community at the highest level. Our area deserves an active, present and hard-working MP. I take this seriously, and have pushed for infrastructure improvements for those affected by flooding, safer rail crossings, more community spaces and more."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6qfn",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Deliver quality, affordable housing alongside the infrastructure needed, including stormwater."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6qhi",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Tackle rising prices: 3 free GP visits, $20 public transport cap, banning price gouging and more."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6qjd",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Protect and expand community spaces to support our growing population, including Pt Chev Bowls Club."
     }
    ],
